/-!
# A covering set on the colimit site of the system of base changes (Stacks 0GN3 at Stacks 03Q6)

This file exhibits a *covering set* in the sense of Stacks 0GN3 on the colimit site of the system
of base changes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/EtaleCohomology/Colimits/QcqsBaseChangeEtaleCohomology.lean` — a
set `S` of sheaves of sets which covers the final sheaf, is stable under lifting surjections,
under products and under equalizers, and all of whose members are quasi-compact — and discharges
all five of its conditions. The conclusion of Stacks 0GN3 for that site, with nothing assumed
beyond the source's own hypotheses, is
`isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_bc`.

**It does not unlock Stacks 03Q6, and the `@[stacks 03Q6]` strings say so.** The whole 0GN3/0GN4
family concludes about `CategoryTheory.Limits.colimit G` for an honest filtered diagram
`G : I ⥤ Sheaf J Ab`, and this development has no such diagram: `colim_i f_i⁻¹F_i` is pinned only
by the universal property
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSiteCohomology.IsColimitPresentation` and realised by
`systemColimitSheaf` as a pointwise left Kan extension, the diagram `i ↦ f_i⁻¹F_i` not being
available as a functor at all. That obstruction is prior to any covering set.

Nor does it unlock the *other* route, `Stacks.Cohomology.CechComplexExactPos` for the colimit
sheaf — condition (2) of Stacks 07A1 and the one input of
`Stacks.WeakSites.ColimitSiteCohomology.isZero_rightDerivedΓ_of_pointwise_injective`. It does
not;
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/Acyclicity/CoveringSetAcyclicity.lean` explains
why in full and proves what a covering set *does* give. The decisive point is that
`Stacks.Cohomology.isTotallyAcyclic_of_conditions` does not need arbitrary surjections at all: it
applies condition (2) exactly once, to the one surjection
`Stacks.Cohomology.exists_epi_subsingleton_ext` hands it, and in that application the acyclicity
of the Cech terms in every degree below the top is already supplied by the induction hypothesis.
So condition (2) contributes only the top degree, which is the degree the induction is trying to
reach — it is an induction-breaking input of the same strength as the conclusion, not a
quasi-compactness statement in disguise. What the covering set gives is acyclicity of the sheaf on
every member of `S`, which is condition (1) restated and not condition (2). So this file stands on
its own as Stacks 0GN4 at this site.

## The site, and the choice of `S`

The colimit site is `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.AffineLimitCohomology.limitSite` at the system of
base changes, that is `bcLimitSiteGen`: the small **affine** etale site of the limit `Y = cY.pt`,
with its morphism universe raised by `CategoryTheory.AsSmall`, carrying the topology generated by
`bcPrecoverageGen`. Its objects are the affine schemes etale over `Y`; its coverings are the
*finite* jointly surjective etale families, finiteness being part of
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallAffineEtale.IsCovering`.

The set taken here is the one of Stacks 0GN4: the finite coproducts
`∐_{i = 1, …, n} h_{U_i}^♯` of sheafified representables of objects `U_i` of a collection
`B ⊆ Ob(C)`, i.e. `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.FiniteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda`, with

> `B = Set.univ`: **all** objects of the colimit site.

That choice is forced, and the two obvious alternatives both fail, for reasons worth recording
because they are what makes this a real question rather than bookkeeping.

* `B = ∅`, or any `B` not covering `Y`, makes condition (1) of Stacks 0GN4 false rather than
  vacuous: condition (1) *is* the assertion that the members of `B` cover the final sheaf, so a
  degenerate `B` does not trivialise the hypotheses, it destroys one of them. There is therefore
  no vacuity to guard against here.
* `B = {`objects attached to the affine **opens** of `Y``}` — the Zariski choice, which is what
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.AffineEtaleTopOneHypercover` builds for the degree-zero Cech step —
  satisfies conditions (1), (3) and (4) of Stacks 0GN4 comfortably: (1) is a finite affine open
  cover, (3) is quasi-separatedness of `Y` in the shape of
  `Stacks.QcqsOneHypercover.exists_finite_affine_oneHypercover_opens`, and (4) is free because an
  open immersion is a monomorphism, so there is at most one morphism between two members and the
  equalizer of a parallel pair is the whole source. It fails condition (2): a covering of an
  affine open of `Y` in the *etale* topology cannot be refined by a Zariski cover. And condition
  (2) is not an artifact of the reduction — it is what produces hypothesis (2) of Stacks 0GN3,
  the lifting of surjections, and that hypothesis genuinely fails for the Zariski set, a sheaf
  surjecting onto `h_U^♯` having sections only etale-locally.

## How the five conditions are discharged

Only quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `X ⟶ T`, the source's own hypothesis on `X`, is
used, and only through the limit: `compactSpace_limit_baseChange` and
`quasiSeparatedSpace_limit_baseChange` make `Y` a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme, the legs
of the limit cone of a system with affine transitions being affine.

1. `bcCoversTop_univ`. Finitely many objects whose sheafified representables cover the final
   sheaf: the objects attached to a finite affine open cover of `Y`. This is the `coversTop` field
   of `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.AffineEtaleTopOneHypercover.exists_finite_isTopOneHypercover`, read
   at the small model `AsSmall.down`.
2. `bcHasFiniteCoverRefinements_univ`. Every covering sieve of every object is refined by a finite
   covering family. The coverings of the small affine etale site are finite by definition, so this
   is `AlgebraicGeometry.finite_refinement_smallAffineEtale` transported across the universe raise
   by `CategoryTheory.AsSmall.mem_comap_toGrothendieck_iff`. The `∀ i, V i ∈ B` clause is where
   `B = Set.univ` is used, and it is the reason no smaller `B` will do. No hypothesis on `X` at
   all.
3. `bcProduct_univ`. The fibre product `U ×_Y U'` of the schemes of two objects is **not** an
   object — the site has fibre products over its own objects
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.hasPullbacks_smallAffineEtale`, a fibre product of affines over an affine
   being affine), but this product is over `Y`, which is an object only when `Y` is affine, and
   `U ×_Y U'` for two affine schemes etale over a non-affine `Y` need not be affine, two affine
   opens of a non-separated scheme having non-affine intersection. So the `V_i` are the objects
   attached to a finite affine open cover of that fibre product, which exists because it is
   quasi-compact (`compactSpace_prodScheme`: `U' ⟶ Y` is quasi-compact by
   `AlgebraicGeometry.quasiCompact_of_compactSpace`, `U'` being affine and `Y` quasi-separated,
   hence so is its base change) and quasi-separated (`isSeparated_prodScheme`: it is separated
   over the affine `U`). A pair of morphisms into `U` and `U'` induces a morphism into the fibre
   product, and over an affine open of the source inside the preimage of a member of the cover it
   factors — `exists_prodCover_factorization`. The jointly surjective family of those affine opens
   generates a covering sieve by `mem_toGrothendieck_ofArrows_up`.
4. `bcEqualizer_univ`, with **one** object and **no** covering at all. The equalizer of
   `a, b : U ⟶ U'` taken in `Over Y` includes into `U` by a morphism that is an open immersion —
   the diagonal of the etale `U' ⟶ Y` is one, `AlgebraicGeometry.isOpenImmersion_equalizer_ι_left`
   — and a closed immersion — `U' ⟶ Y` is separated, `U'` being affine, so Mathlib's
   `AlgebraicGeometry.isClosedImmersion_equalizer_ι_left` applies. Being closed in the affine `U`
   its source is affine, is contained in `B` by `Scheme.size_lt_of_isClosedImmersion`, and is
   etale over `Y`: an object of the site, `equalizerObj`. An equalizing morphism then factors
   through it by the universal property, `equalizerLift`, so the covering sieve exhibited is `⊤`.
   No quasi-compactness and no quasi-separatedness of anything is used.
5. `isQuasiCompact_mem_bcCoveringSet`. Every member of `S` is a quasi-compact sheaf: condition (2)
   fed to
   `Stacks.Cohomology.ColimitsOfCohomology.isQuasiCompact_of_finiteCoproductSheafifiedYoneda`.

The two sheaf-theoretic reductions that turn (3) and (4) into the hom-set statements proved here
are available: `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_prodLift_of_exists_covering` and
`…_equalizerLift_of_exists_covering`.

## Main definitions

* `objOfEtale`: **an affine scheme of `B` with an etale morphism to `S` is an object of the small
  affine etale site of `S`** — the common generalisation of
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.QcqsLimitCohomology.objOfAffineOpen` and of
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.AffineEtaleTopOneHypercover.objOfOpenOver`, both of which ask their
  scheme to be an open of something already in the site. Conditions (3) and (4) both need objects
  that are neither.
* `equalizerObj`, `equalizerHom`, `equalizerLift`: the equalizer of a parallel pair as an object
  of the site, its inclusion, and the factorisation of an equalizing morphism through it.
* `prodScheme`, `prodObj`, `prodObjFst`, `prodObjSnd`, `prodLiftScheme`: the fibre product of the
  schemes of two objects, the object attached to an affine open of it, its two projections, and
  the morphism into it induced by a pair.
* `bcCoveringSet`: the covering set `S` on the colimit site — the finite coproducts of sheafified
  representables of **all** objects of that site.

## Main results

* `quasiSeparatedSpace_baseChange_obj`, `compactSpace_limit_baseChange`,
  `quasiSeparatedSpace_limit_baseChange`: the limit `Y` of the system of base changes is a
  quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme when `X ⟶ T` is quasi-compact and quasi-separated.
* `exists_prodCover_factorization`: condition (3) of Stacks 0GN4 at the level of the site, for an
  arbitrary quasi-compact quasi-separated base.
* `mem_toGrothendieck_ofArrows_up`: a jointly surjective family of objects over an object of the
  colimit site generates a covering sieve of it.
* `bcCoversTop_univ`, `bcHasFiniteCoverRefinements_univ`, `bcProduct_univ`, `bcEqualizer_univ`:
  **the four conditions of Stacks 0GN4 for `B = Set.univ`.**
* `isQuasiCompact_mem_bcCoveringSet`: hypothesis (5) of Stacks 0GN3 for `bcCoveringSet`.
* `isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_bc`: **Stacks 0GN3 on the colimit site of the
  system of base changes, with no covering-set hypothesis left.**

## Implementation notes

The index types of Stacks 0GN4's conditions are `Fin m`, while the geometry produces a `Finite`
index type in `Type`; `Finite.equivFin` reindexes. The reindexing is done on the *opens* rather
than on the objects, because `x ∈ O (e.symm (e k))` is a proposition and `rw` can rewrite inside
it, whereas reindexing a family of objects changes the type of a morphism out of it and the
rewrite motive stops being type-correct.

The universe raise costs almost nothing. A morphism `AsSmall.up.obj A ⟶ W` of the raised site is
by definition a `ULift` of a morphism `A ⟶ AsSmall.down.obj W`, so families produced downstairs
are lifted by `ULift.up` with no `eqToHom`, and `AsSmall.down.map ⟨f⟩ = f` holds by `rfl`. Where
`AsSmall.up` appears with no expected type to pin its universe parameter, the sieve is taken from
`mem_toGrothendieck_ofArrows_up` rather than written out, which pins it.

The inclusion of the equalizer and the factorisation through it are given names
(`equalizerι`, `equalizerιLift`) with their domain and codomain ascribed through
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallAffineEtale.toScheme` rather than left at the `Over S` spelling
`(overObj _).left`. The two are the same scheme, but only definitionally, and instance search does
not find `Etale (structMap _)` at the second spelling.

